cerberust

This project's design was inspired by Protect AI's llm-guard
(https://github.com/protectai/llm-guard), a Python toolkit for securing LLM
input and output. cerberust borrows concepts — the scanner/vault model, the
reversible-redaction approach, and the prompt-injection classifier
(protectai/deberta-v3-base-prompt-injection-v2) — but shares no source code with
it. We credit llm-guard as prior art with thanks.

Third-party data
----------------

src/scanner/gitleaks_rules.rs is generated from the default configuration of
gitleaks v8.30.1 (https://github.com/gitleaks/gitleaks), vendored unmodified in
data/gitleaks/gitleaks.toml. gitleaks is MIT-licensed, Copyright (c) 2019
Zachary Rice; see data/gitleaks/LICENSE.

data/bip39/english.txt is the BIP-0039 English wordlist
(https://github.com/bitcoin/bips), MIT-licensed; see data/bip39/LICENSE.
